    "author": "Codex",
    "entrance": "Upper west shelf beside the guard-loaded long spring.",
    "exit": "Upper west gallery above the starting shelf, opened by cargo delivered from the east.",
    "solution": "Let the guard depress the long spring, then go past him alive and cross the lowered passage. A standing spring would leave only an eight-pixel crack beneath that roof. Jump up to retrieve the far lantern, bring it back through the passage, and throw it left into the low brass pocket. Its weight opens the high west exit, independently of the knight. Now jump over the guard and use two low downward cuts. The fatal cut releases the spring. Steer toward its western edge as it rises under you, catch the lift, then jump left around the canopy into the upper gallery. The same floor first enables the cargo journey and then closes that route while lifting you to the return exit.",
    "nearestExisting": "The rejected B42 was only defeat enemy, catch spring, leave. This version gives the live weight a job that must remain useful during a whole cargo round trip: lowering a corridor to the distant lantern. The returning spring reverses that job and becomes the high return launch only after the cargo is independently stored.",
    "novelty": "A living enemy is useful infrastructure before it is a rebound target. The spring changes the topology of the same passage: keep it down to fetch and return the remote weight, then release it to close the route behind you and reach the higher way home.",
    "requiredEvents": [
      "pickup",
      "throw",
      "held-open",
      "pogo-low",
      "enemy-defeat",
      "recoil-jump"
    ],
    "humanReview": "User rejected the overhead bypass and the simple enemy-to-spring demonstration. Reinvented as an out-and-back cargo puzzle where killing the weight prematurely closes the essential passage. Awaiting review.",
