    "designNotes": "The roof is continuous with the top boundary, so the old over-the-guard bypass is gone. More importantly, the room is now an out-and-back spatial dependency rather than a capped version of the old jump. The long spring is a corridor floor while depressed and seals that corridor at rest. The guard keeps it depressed while the knight retrieves distant cargo; manual depression after an early kill cannot remain loaded during that long walk. The west pressure pocket has a fixed end wall so the thrown lantern settles securely. No hidden event receipts control the exit. Low cuts are the forgiving demonstrated combat route; ordinary combat and emergent alternatives retain their existing rules.",
